{
 "id": "AT-M3-14c-c8-rare",
 "needs": [
  "types"
 ],
 "note": "AT-M3-14 (F), C8: smoke fails C8 only when the count of a rare string (a baseline count that is a whole number from 1 to c8.rare_max) changes, up or down; a common word's changed count is an `info c8` line and smoke stays green. The baseline as recorded (on Claude Code 2.1.325, where the compaction experiment's flag and env variable carry a whole prompt, not an arm name) has no arm list and no common word: (a) checks that shape (0 common words) and that the pass line names no arm list, and (c) to (e) run on it as recorded. fake-claude.pl writes a stand-in binary (2.1.999: smoke takes a version-named binary's name; it exits 0 for validate and test) holding every baseline string as often as the baseline counts it, then shifts the most frequent string, drops or adds one of the least frequent, or appends the old arm list and arm names; no string is named here, each is picked from the staged baseline. The case runs on its own staged copy (stage_overlay with the baseline as staged) so steps (b) and (f) to (n) can edit the baseline (baseline-edit.pl), (b) only after (e): one below the highest count makes the most frequent string common, a string whose count equals it is rare, and without the key every count of 1 or more is rare, as with a malformed one (i: -1, j: not a number); (f) rare_max 0 and (f2) a rare_max below every count leave no rare string, so C8 fails with a line that says so (it would compare nothing); (o) to (q2) a count of 0, which is never rare and which the tool never writes (one among rare counts, one beside counts above rare_max, every count, and every count under --skip-cli), fails C8 and names it, though the stand-in matches every count; (l) to (n) a baseline with a count that is not a whole number, no counts (under --skip-cli too) or no c8 part fails C8 with a line that says so. (r) and (r2) start again from the baseline as recorded (copied at (a)) and add a count for an empty string, which only a hand edit can hold: C8 fails with a line that says so before any count is read (with --skip-cli too), where it once searched the binary for the empty string without end. A pass line names the rare and common counts baseline-edit.pl count reads from the staged baseline",
 "now": "2026-10-21T14:05:12+03:00",
 "tz": "Etc/GMT-3",
 "env": {
  "CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR": "$TMP/cct"
 },
 "stage_overlay": {
  "assets/canary-baseline.json": "$PLUGIN/assets/canary-baseline.json"
 },
 "steps": [
  {
   "name": "(a) a baseline with no arm list and no common word (the shape recorded on Claude Code 2.1.325), every count as recorded: C8 passes, its pass line names no arm list, no info line, smokeDue cleared",
   "setup": [
    {
     "write": "$WATCH/version.json",
     "json": {
      "lastVersion": "2.1.999",
      "smokeDue": "2.1.999"
     }
    },
    {
     "copy": "$PLUGIN/assets/canary-baseline.json",
     "to": "$TMP/baseline-as-recorded.json"
    }
   ],
   "exec": [
    "/usr/bin/perl",
    "$CASE/fake-claude.pl",
    "$PLUGIN/assets/canary-baseline.json",
    "$TMP/v/2.1.999"
   ],
   "expect": {
    "exit": 0
   }
  },
  {
   "exec": [
    "/usr/bin/perl",
    "$CASE/baseline-edit.pl",
    "$PLUGIN/assets/canary-baseline.json",
    "shape"
   ],
   "expect": {
    "exit": 0,
    "stdout_has": [
     "^arm_list absent\\n\\z"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "exec": [
    "/usr/bin/perl",
    "$CASE/baseline-edit.pl",
    "$PLUGIN/assets/canary-baseline.json",
    "count"
   ],
   "expect": {
    "exit": 0,
    "stdout_has": [
     "^rare [1-9]\\d* common 0$"
    ]
   },
   "capture": {
    "C8_RARE": "re:^rare (\\d+) common \\d+$",
    "C8_COMMON": "re:^rare \\d+ common (\\d+)$"
   }
  },
  {
   "argv": [
    "smoke",
    "--sid",
    "$SID",
    "--claude",
    "$TMP/v/2.1.999",
    "--types",
    "$TYPES"
